module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.test_identity_restated_as_a_location_predicate_beside_the_marker

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data test_identity_restated_as_a_location_predicate_beside_the_marker: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "test_identity_restated_as_a_location_predicate_beside_the_marker" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a test is a declaration carrying the authored `test` marker and nothing else, but the native lane restated that identity as a LOCATION predicate beside it (the module's namespace had to be `v2.test` or below, spelled twice: once where the universe was derived and once where the receipt was judged, plus a hand-mirrored copy of the default pattern in the seed) -- so a marked declaration outside the predicate was silently not a test and a module named inside it was a test candidate whatever it contained (INVALID STATE: two authorities for one fact, `what is a test`, which disagree on every marked declaration outside `v2.test` and are checked against each other by nothing).**",
    "REPAIR LANDED WITH THIS ROW (source layout authority, audit item 2): the universe is the marked declarations of the acquired modules and the pattern only SELECTS within it by label; the two namespace predicates are deleted; the default pattern is the route boundary `//v2/...` and is the only place the boundary is spelled; a duplicate (module, declaration) marker identity and a marked declaration no label can name refuse the lane; the enumeration of a single named namespace is deleted with its claims. Controls: `test.claim.native_lane_universe_selection` (marked outside `v2.test`, unmarked inside it, duplicate marker identity, a malformed module holding a marker-shaped spelling refused rather than read as zero tests) and `v2.test.v2_native_route` (the boundary, the entries, the nonempty-where-required contract through `an_empty_universe_is_refused`).",
    "RESIDUAL, NOT REPAIRED HERE -- the same fork one level out, in the ROUTES rather than the lane: a marked declaration in a module under `dag/test/manual/` is selected by neither route. The native lane's boundary is the `v2` namespace; `gunbc.discovery_census` `claim_route_universe` is the `//test/claim/...` label subtree; and `test/manual/` is a declared `OfflineLocalRecipe` exclusion of the required floor (`gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots`), whose own dissolution is that the manual suites migrate under `test/claim` with declared consumers. A declaration there that carries the marker is therefore a test that no `gunbc test` operand reaches -- a test-loss gap, whose population is re-derivable as the marked declarations of the modules `git ls-files dag/test/manual` lists. It is not closed by one value: the claim route executes the sites discovery enumerates, and discovery excludes `test/manual/` by that declared row, so a `//test/...` operand would admit labels whose population discovery has excluded by declaration -- an operand that selects nothing silently, or a new typed refusal, and in either case a decision on the offline recipes that a widened pattern value does not make. The widening is therefore the capability named below, not a change to the universe value.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- nothing refused the disagreement. The universe was a filter on top of the marker, so the lane answered a smaller question than the marker defines and reported it as the whole, and the receipt clause that should have caught a member outside the universe was the same predicate spelled a second time.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed for the lane (the marker is the only input to identity, so no namespace predicate has a constructor in the universe derivation; the duplicate and unlabelable marker shapes are typed refusals at derivation). The route-level residual above is decidable and its ceiling is the same once the claim executor's population is defined; it is below ceiling today.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: the claim route enumerates every marked declaration of the modules its operand reaches -- a population defined by the marker through the same acquired-module fold the native lane uses -- sufficient for `gunbc test` over `//test/...` to select, run or refuse each marked declaration of `dag/test/manual/` and to leave every unmarked declaration out, with the offline-recipe exclusion stated as a typed refusal of that selection and not as a missing route.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.witness.v2_native_route", decl_name: "native_route_default_pattern", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.discovery_census", decl_name: "claim_route_universe", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.compile", decl_name: "native_lane_universe_selected", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
